From fb36e85b8c7a1b49aa2da5d0fc66a8c4b0c10205 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:58:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MaxCam: cinema camera app for iPhone 17 / iOS 26
 (AVFoundation public APIs)

First-run milestone: real camera preview + Custom Camera Capabilities
diagnostic screen that enumerates exactly what the physical device exposes.

Highlights:
- Capability engine: DeviceCapabilities/CameraFormatInfo snapshots from
  AVCaptureDevice.DiscoverySession; no model hard-coding.
- CapabilityMatrix builds only configurations the active format advertises,
  including Apple Log 2 (.appleLog2, iOS 26) and native ProRes 422 HQ when
  AVCaptureMovieFileOutput advertises it (<=30fps, DeviceCapabilities gated).
- CameraEngine (thread-safe final class): HEVC Main10 recording via
  AVAssetWriter with honest BT.2020 color metadata for Log/HLG; Open Gate via
  setDynamicAspectRatio (iOS 26+); Pro Video Storage opt-in only on iOS 27+;
  manual ISO/exposure/bias, focus lock, temperature/tint white balance.
- MetalProcessor + MaxCamShaders.metal optional display-transform preview with
  graceful fallback when no metallib is present.
- DiagnosticsExport report + share sheet; CapabilityGate reasons for every
  unsupported option; pure-Swift CapabilityGateTests unit-test target.
- Shared scheme with TestAction; pbxproj validated (68 objects, no undefined
  refs) via scripts/validate_pbxproj.py.

Verification on Linux is static only (no Swift toolchain); unit tests require
Xcode/macOS.
